SUMMARY:Lancaster-Lebanon Watershed Forum
DESCRIPTION:The 2026 Lancaster-Lebanon Watershed Forum will be held on Saturday\, November 7 from 8:30 AM – 12:00 PM at Elizabethtown College! This free event is a great opportunity for watershed protection volunteers and professionals to learn\, discuss issues\, and share ideas. \nRegistration is free but required. Please register by October 30: https://forms.gle/LGqDPbGsW7UXCLhe8
URL:https://lancasterwatersheds.org/event/2026-lancaster-lebanon-watershed-forum/
LOCATION:Elizabethtown College\, Susquehanna Room\, 1 Alpha Drive\, Elizabethtown\, PA\, 17022\, United States
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Lancaster Watersheds
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20261112T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261112T150000
DTSTAMP:20261010T013201
CREATED:20261009T191233Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20261009T191233Z
UID:15064-1794474000-1794495600@lancasterwatersheds.org
SUMMARY:
DESCRIPTION:We have a training opportunity to offer. As Lancaster county continues to ramp up and support restoration efforts\, our team sees value in equally scaling up monitoring capacity. To support data collection efforts\, WQMAT is partnering with PA DEP to host a training with DEP’s Melissa Harrison covering macroinvertebrate collection\, habitat assessment\, and field meter calibration. All of which are crucial when collecting in-stream data that will be considered ‘high quality’ or Tier 3 via DEP’s monitoring standards and protocols. \nAs you know\, DEP has a tiered system for quality of data submitted to their bi-annual Integrated Report\, Tier 3 being the highest\, and that is also what’s required for data to be considered for any stream delisting purposes. Folks who attend this training should have the intent to then complete an audit through DEP to be officially considered a Tier 3 data collector.  \nPlease plan to bring your own lunch for this event. \nPlease RSVP: WQMAT DEP Tier 3 Certification for in-stream monitoring \nContact: noellelafaver@lancasterconservation.org or sthomas@chesapeakeconservancy.org
URL:https://lancasterwatersheds.org/event/15064/
LOCATION:Silver Mine Park\, 99 Silver Mine Road\, Pequea\, PA\, 17565\, United States
END:VEVENT
